SELECT * FROM IdentityDirectoryEvents LIMIT 5;
]

Thought: AlertInfo doesn’t have a Description field, but it does have Title and other meta fields. I’ll search AlertInfo titles for “SID history” to locate the alert corresponding to the SID history injection attack. Once I find it, I’ll use its AlertId or time window to correlate with process data (likely in DeviceProcessEvents) to identify the process file name involved.

Action: execute[
SELECT *
FROM AlertInfo
WHERE Title LIKE '%SID history%' OR Title LIKE '%SID History%';
]

Thought: No matching records for Emma Clark were found in the interactive SigninLogs. Since the question is about a suspected overpass-the-hash (Kerberos) attack, it might involve non-interactive/AAD token usage. I should therefore search in AADNonInteractiveUserSignInLogs (and possibly other AAD-related tables) for an account corresponding to Emma Clark, then extract the UserId (AAD User ID) from there.

