]

Thought: The previous query failed because the SigninLogs table doesn’t have a column named `Username`. I should (a) inspect the schema of SigninLogs to see the exact column names, then (b) query using valid user-related fields (typically `UserPrincipalName`, `UserDisplayName`, maybe `UserId`) and IP column (commonly `IPAddress`). Once I find the sign-in event for user `kyleg` from IP `35.202.74.47`, I can pivot to related alerts (SecurityAlert/AlertInfo/AlertEvidence) and then to DeviceProcessEvents to find the credential theft tool process and its executable file name.

